        <div><a name="_manchu" id="_manchu"></a><p class="h2Annex">C.30 Manchu</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_6785d2fb-e71e-42fa-a4d9-1cb36ad50940" id="_6785d2fb-e71e-42fa-a4d9-1cb36ad50940"></a>name components:</p>

  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo32;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">
    family name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo32;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">
    given name
  </p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_0c73b056-3ca6-4e3d-8b52-1ddb564e5840" id="_0c73b056-3ca6-4e3d-8b52-1ddb564e5840"></a>Manchus are called only by their given names.
Manchu clan names (&#x201C;hala&#x201D;) are not used with their personal names,
but occasionally a family name is used.</p>
<div><a name="_typical_name_patterns_10" id="_typical_name_patterns_10"></a><p class="h3Annex">C.30.1 Typical name patterns</p><p class="TableTitle" align="center">Table C.40</p><div align="center"><table style="mso-table-lspace:15.0cm;margin-left:423.0pt;mso-table-rspace:15.0cm;margin-right:423.0pt;mso-table-bspace:14.2pt;mso-table-anchor-vertical:paragraph;mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;" class="MsoISOTable" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"><a name="_5b4b9006-0b59-4e2b-adaf-69d222e9ec4d" id="_5b4b9006-0b59-4e2b-adaf-69d222e9ec4d"></a><tbody><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">given name</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
